---
import Diagram from '../Diagram.astro';
---
<Diagram caption="Instant Recovery changes where the VM runs before it changes where the data lives. Migrate to production copies the blocks in the background, and the repository leaves the I/O path when that copy finishes.">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="irTitle irDesc">
    <title id="irTitle">The VM's I/O path during and after Instant Recovery</title>
    <desc id="irDesc">
      While running from the backup, the Hyper-V VM does its I/O against the backup repository
      and production storage is not yet in use, so the VM is up in minutes with limited
      performance. After migration to production, the VM uses production storage and the
      repository is out of the I/O path, ready for the VM to be protected as a Hyper-V VM.
    </desc>

    <!-- RUNNING FROM THE BACKUP -->
    <rect class="panel" x="16" y="14" width="320" height="310" rx="12" />
    <text class="panel-title" x="36" y="40">RUNNING FROM THE BACKUP</text>

    <rect class="node" x="106" y="58" width="140" height="42" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="176" y="85" text-anchor="middle">Hyper-V VM</text>

    <path class="link-active" d="M140 100 L140 150 L106 150 L106 186" />
    <text class="tag" x="36" y="136">VM I/O</text>
    <path class="link-dim" d="M212 100 L212 150 L250 150 L250 186" />

    <rect class="node-edge" x="36" y="186" width="140" height="58" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="106" y="212" text-anchor="middle">Repository</text>
    <text class="sub" x="106" y="230" text-anchor="middle">in the I/O path</text>

    <rect class="node" x="182" y="186" width="140" height="58" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="252" y="212" text-anchor="middle">Production</text>
    <text class="sub" x="252" y="230" text-anchor="middle">not in use yet</text>

    <text class="sub" x="36" y="280">Up in minutes, with limited performance.</text>
    <text class="sub" x="36" y="298">A temporary spare, not a finished move.</text>

    <!-- arrow between panels -->
    <path class="link-active" d="M348 170 L376 170" />
    <path class="link-active" d="M368 163 L376 170 L368 177" />

    <!-- ON PRODUCTION STORAGE -->
    <rect class="panel" x="388" y="14" width="316" height="310" rx="12" />
    <text class="panel-title" x="408" y="40">ON PRODUCTION STORAGE</text>

    <rect class="node" x="476" y="58" width="140" height="42" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="546" y="85" text-anchor="middle">Hyper-V VM</text>

    <path class="link-dim" d="M510 100 L510 150 L476 150 L476 186" />
    <path class="link-active" d="M582 100 L582 150 L620 150 L620 186" />
    <text class="tag" x="632" y="136">VM I/O</text>

    <rect class="node" x="406" y="186" width="140" height="58" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="476" y="212" text-anchor="middle">Repository</text>
    <text class="sub" x="476" y="230" text-anchor="middle">out of the path</text>

    <rect class="node-edge" x="552" y="186" width="140" height="58" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="622" y="212" text-anchor="middle">Production</text>
    <text class="sub" x="622" y="230" text-anchor="middle">in the I/O path</text>

    <text class="sub" x="408" y="280">Full performance, no backup dependency.</text>
    <text class="sub" x="408" y="298">Now protect it again as a Hyper-V VM.</text>
  </svg>
</Diagram>
